<h2>Sunday, July 11,  2004</h2>	
<div class="post">
	 <h3 class="storytitle" id="post-30"><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/index.php?p=30" rel="bookmark" title="Permanent Link: Beyond Justice">Beyond Justice</a></h3>
	<div class="meta">posted by: Mark @ 8:58 pm </div>
	
	<div id="wplinks" class="storycontent">
			<p>I was reminded today of a sermon I gave while I was attending a small church on the East Coast.  I hadn&#8217;t been attending that church very long when the Pastor asked if I would preach on a Sunday morning.  As I was trying to figure out what to speak on, a song started playing from a Susan Ashton CD I was listening to called &#8220;Beyond Justice to Mercy".  The song really spoke to me and before I knew it, I had a sermon prepared.   It was my very first time preaching in front of a church, so I wrote everything out and pretty much read from the paper.  My mind tends to go blank when I speak in front of a lot of people, so writing it down gave me some comfort.  Anyways, I thought I&#8217;d post that sermon on here.  </p>
	<p><a href="http://www.marksportal.net/beyondjustice.html">Beyond Justice</a></p>
	<p>Enjoy!
</p>
